PAI 4.0 for QFX5120-48T-6C (BCM84894 "blackfin" copper gearbox).

Source changes only -- all build flags are supplied by common/phy/Makefile,
which scopes every BASE-T/BCM84894 define to the blackfin conditional block so
that Agera3 and Barchetta, which share this PAI, compile exactly as before.

 - address each BCM84894 lane as an independently MDIO-addressable core
   (package_base + local_lane); without this only one core per package is
   configured, so 7 of every 8 copper ports stay down. Gated at runtime on
   BRCM_PAI_BFIN_SUPPORT(chip_name).
 - accept SAI_SWITCH_ATTR_MEDIA_TYPE and SAI_PORT_ATTR_FEC_MODE=NONE, and
   default the system-side interface type to XFI, on BASE-T. Left at NONE the
   speed set maps to bcm_pm_InterfaceKR and the MAC sees a permanent local
   fault. Both gated on BRCM_PAI_BFIN_SUPPORT(chip_name).
 - raise the copper per-package port limit from a hardcoded 1 to the device's
   reported lane count. max_lanes is read back from the PHY immediately above
   the check, so this is identical to the previous behaviour on single-lane
   parts, and the branch is entered only for xgbaset/1G copper PHYs.
 - accept SAI_SWITCH_ATTR_FIRMWARE_PATH_NAME on BCM84894 instead of rejecting
   it, so orchagent can select the INTERNAL firmware load method from
   gearbox_config.json. PAI loads driver-embedded firmware and ignores the
   path, but rejecting it fails create_switch. chip_name is not resolved until
   after the attribute loop, so the case only records the attribute index and
   the BRCM_PAI_BFIN_SUPPORT(chip_name) test is applied once the chip is
   known; every other PHY keeps the original rejection, unchanged.
 - route EXT_MDIO_READ/WRITE to the CL45 entry points. This is reached only
   when EXT_MDIO_APIS is defined, which the Makefile now does solely for
   blackfin builds; without it the vendor's CL22 mapping is unchanged.
 - guard the Aperta MACsec warm-shutdown with PLP_MACSEC_SUPPORT so the call
   is not compiled in when MACsec support is absent.

